{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0124","billNumberShort":"S.B. 124","billNumberLong":"SB0124S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0293","shortTitle":"Child Welfare Modifications","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"ESCAML","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Escamilla, Luz","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"WATKICF","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Watkins, Christine F.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses protective custody warrants and child safety warrants relating to child welfare.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions regarding the issuance of warrants by a juvenile court;<hr><ltbullet>distinguishes between a protective custody warrant and a child safety warrant;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a juvenile court to issue a child safety warrant related to the health, safety, or welfare of a child;<hr><ltbullet>states that a peace officer or child welfare caseworker who is executing a protective custody warrant or a child safety warrant may request assistance in executing the warrant;<hr><ltbullet>specifies that a child safety warrant does not give a peace officer or child welfare caseworker authority to take a child into protective custody;<hr><ltbullet>defines terms; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kami Orton","fiscalAnalyst":"Kevin Edminster","lastAction":"Senate/ filed","lastActionOwner":"Senate file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"NYBKDFVPIP","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-12 15:30:38.720","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-12 15:30:38.720","actionC